#edb/ref 17592186285918} {:answer/id #uuid "ece98db4-8fb5-5de6-96ae-eab2daaf204e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286956} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bbdf96-652e-5a44-8baa-16e0b9ca543f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287063} {:answer/id #uuid "fb59feea-37b5-52e5-9084-42c7ddf769da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb59feea-37b5-52e5-9084-42c7ddf769da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287081} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ac708a-11ad-565c-8322-1d93c1389c6f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "576083d0-69bc-5a44-8497-3c93280947cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181600" :question/problem "![](images/83/83ebd6f5d742a869b267a0cead4a9a94ae17fa534ca3e1cfddbb495c67390ecf.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x$ and *below* the line $y=2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=-x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x\\le y<2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\le y<2\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46af21cb-361b-5fb4-ab1d-162f6dc19fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46af21cb-361b-5fb4-ab1d-162f6dc19fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285439} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b2e6e8-e3a7-5dc9-8ac1-fe4ec9a406fe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "750ca960-2d08-58a0-966e-64431106cace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "750ca960-2d08-58a0-966e-64431106cace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285868} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fafe7ac-dbc0-5cdf-bc0c-5c63228b3957" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8932e43d-7f5d-54b2-a7c5-53ff42abdde0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8932e43d-7f5d-54b2-a7c5-53ff42abdde0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286045} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bf54d46-5083-5c2f-b1b8-5402c86f58b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dedb72cf-47cf-5e98-a478-6359d9544476" :question/math-academy-id "q-181610" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fbd778f48199acd5b731e739cb527a990ba28a8d88981d50554d135e853f8815.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$36$\n\n$\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=3$ and vertical radius $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n4(0)^{2}+9(0)^{2}\\,<\\,36.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<36.\n$$\n\nNotice that we use $<$ since the boundary is excluded from the set (the boundary curve is dashed).\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<36\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e53d49-a131-5b22-8032-7c46e048c20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284843} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a41c1-c4b5-5356-bfa1-c588f3dcba2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285158} {:answer/id #uuid "365c747b-3953-581f-aef5-c73b4645b4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285290} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d59a60-cd9b-516f-b633-35c498b446d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286574} {:answer/id #uuid "e0557cc8-7b4f-5837-9792-b28c8c976daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "365c747b-3953-581f-aef5-c73b4645b4e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285290} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c3edeea-b9cb-5e83-ac25-cc33de1ab2d7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e9760d-e45c-5051-bbd0-2a36daa0f878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284831} {:answer/id #uuid "1cee33e7-f890-5d46-8dbc-785458ae8d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285048} {:answer/id #uuid "1df4b5c4-3a35-5669-a09b-485943319faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175