 #edb/ref 17592186285321} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab7d9b8-1d47-56d4-a66f-0f80a739dcdf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dab3d6dc-4b31-53f2-8ab3-bc64485c9198" :question/math-academy-id "q-181688" :question/problem "![](images/46/4628a6e45445a585361f7d32586b27e29bc726d4ed8b7f072679e5537df59644.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x+1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,3x\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=x+1$ and *below* the line $y=3x.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>x+1,\\,y<3x.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\nx+1<y<3x.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx+1<y\\le 3x\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+1<y\\le 3x\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198477 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c363dc7-c63c-5ed3-8925-cff2c056e927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284890} {:answer/id #uuid "3c64737d-5d99-51dd-8c6b-8b18ab4caf25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285354} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad2f096-495a-5379-967d-a399be975c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285768} {:answer/id #uuid "78b2d88d-ad88-57e0-a78c-60db54a02e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285911} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5646b7-086f-537d-afba-ae287ac1d4f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ad2f096-495a-5379-967d-a399be975c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285768} :answer-field/id #uuid "298fe454-548d-57b1-83b1-aa9c3c098f58" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36be1f81-762f-5b0f-9e30-f55647bd743a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285300} {:answer/id #uuid "40058a42-af03-5b28-b0f1-312ed2ee0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285386} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7232cb-ed44-5bbb-90d1-f788b431742d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285796} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb49ff2-4570-59bf-81b5-723849e9be0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40058a42-af03-5b28-b0f1-312ed2ee0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285386} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58f6ca9-ed1c-51ce-8551-d70b9d506ea5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2547003-ad79-57a3-97bf-c8a4091bfc89" :question/math-academy-id "q-181692" :question/problem "![](images/70/7021cfd590d7e090128061d42c140ab81633f20e8cd1bff60f6252bc8e9aa882.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,-{y}^{2}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *to the right* of the curve $x=-{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx>-{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $x=-{y}^{2}$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge -{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69670d3d-4c35-5e47-ac77-855bbb84bf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285755} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea5b245-1f40-532c-9d05-5940a886593c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value